      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "public-records-appeals",
          "headingId": "public-records-appeals-heading",
          "title": "Public Records Appeals",
          "descriptions": [
            "Decisions and hearing recordings concerning access to American Fork City and AFPD-related records. Summaries describe the records rulings, not findings on the underlying police encounters."
          ],
          "contents": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2026"
            },
            {
              "type": "folder",
              "label": "Adam Williams v. American Fork City — Appeal 2026-235",
              "anchor": "appeal-2026-235",
              "contents": [
                {
                  "type": "formatted-text",
                  "segments": [
                    {
                      "text": "October 27, 2026 — Government Records Office. Williams requested body-worn camera and dash-camera policies, training materials, retention schedules, procedures, and audits. His fee-waiver appeal was denied, but the city was ordered to provide responsive public records upon payment of $61.25, including more than 1,000 pages of training records found in a supplemental search."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "utah-government-records-office-adam-williams-v-american-fork-city-decision-2026-235"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2025"
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "Eric Roundy’s three decisions were issued December 30, 2025. Appeal 2025-105 against Utah County concerned AFPD citation and Spillman records and was denied. Appeal 2025-106 against American Fork City concerned police-encounter records and was denied. Appeal 2025-124 against the city concerned communications with his employer and was partially granted: the city had to provide two additional emails and an itemized receipt for its $200 fee."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "Related encounter: "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "Eric Roundy",
                  "url": "/police-encounters/eric-roundy/?tab=grama-appeals",
                  "same-tab": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "$ref": "entity-folder-tree-eric-roundy-grama-appeals",
              "$path": [
                "contents"
              ],
              "$spread": true
            }
          ]
        },
